      "title": "SQL injection in email search",
      "description": "The index action interpolates the q request parameter straight into the SQL string. Any authenticated caller controls the WHERE clause. A caller can read every column of every user, including api_token, or alter the query freely. Pass the value as a bound parameter and escape the LIKE wildcards.",
      "suggested_change": "    users = users.where(\"email LIKE ?\", \"%#{User.sanitize_sql_like(params[:q])}%\") if params[:q].present?",
      "source": "semgrep:ruby.rails.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The index action interpolates the q request parameter straight into the SQL string. Any authenticated caller controls the WHERE clause.",
      "consequence": "A caller can read every column of every user, including api_token, or alter the query freely.",
      "fix": "Pass the value as a bound parameter and escape the LIKE wildcards."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
