      "title": "Profile update permits every attribute",
      "description": "The profile action permits every key in the user params and writes them all to the record. The caller can therefore set any column, including the admin flag and api_token. Any authenticated user can promote themselves to admin or overwrite their token, which breaks the authorization model. Permit an explicit list of profile fields instead of permitting everything.",
      "suggested_change": "    @current_user.update!(params.require(:user).permit(:email))",
      "source": null,
